From f78b4179d7ac287dad02b6431acb011b71346ee9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Caleb J. Westfall" <calebwestfall1989@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:55:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ProofScope v1.2: countermodel families, Mathlib proof search,
 interacting changes

- Soundness erratum for frozen v1.1: replaced assumptions (drop D, add A) were
  classified separately, giving unsound decisive verdicts (hostile z01, z02, z03,
  z06). adelta12 decides them jointly (mixed_strict, mixed_incomparable,
  mixed_ref_false). No previously reported result is affected.
- lean/ProofScope/CompositionV12.lean: 14 theorems (12 axiom-free, 2 standard).
- proofscope/models.py: countermodel registry (DihedralGroup 3, Finset (Fin 2),
  ZMod 4, ZMod 3, ...) and Mathlib proof portfolio.
- proofscope/adelta12.py: round-robin witness search (v1.1 truncation never
  reached late carriers), literal point pools, joint mixed-change decision.
- proofscope/v12.py: sharded runner, coverage matrix, unsound gate.
- Suites: mathlib_v12_eval (80, frozen, never run), mathlib_v12_dev (5),
  v12_hostile (7); V12_FREEZE.txt. Workflows v12-core and mathlib-v12.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D6eL9tvFdmWVfTWBctgXnC
